    /**
     * Shows a vertical list.
     * 
     * <picture>
     *   <source srcset="https://docs.gtk.org/gtk4/list-box-dark.png" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)">
     *   <img alt="An example GtkListBox" src="https://docs.gtk.org/gtk4/list-box.png">
     * </picture>
     * 
     * A {@link Gtk.ListBox} only contains {@link Gtk.ListBoxRow} children. These rows can
     * by dynamically sorted and filtered, and headers can be added dynamically
     * depending on the row content. It also allows keyboard and mouse navigation
     * and selection like a typical list.
     * 
     * Using {@link Gtk.ListBox} is often an alternative to {@link Gtk.TreeView}, especially
     * when the list contents has a more complicated layout than what is allowed
     * by a {@link Gtk.CellRenderer}, or when the contents is interactive (i.e. has a
     * button in it).
     * 
     * Although a {@link Gtk.ListBox} must have only {@link Gtk.ListBoxRow} children, you can
     * add any kind of widget to it via {@link Gtk.ListBox.prepend},
     * {@link Gtk.ListBox.append} and {@link Gtk.ListBox.insert} and a
     * {@link Gtk.ListBoxRow} widget will automatically be inserted between the list
     * and the widget.
     * 
     * `GtkListBoxRows` can be marked as activatable or selectable. If a row is
     * activatable, `Gtk.ListBox::row-activated` will be emitted for it when
     * the user tries to activate it. If it is selectable, the row will be marked
     * as selected when the user tries to select it.
     * 
     * # GtkListBox as GtkBuildable
     * 
     * The {@link Gtk.ListBox} implementation of the {@link Gtk.Buildable} interface supports
     * setting a child as the placeholder by specifying “placeholder” as the “type”
     * attribute of a `<child>` element. See {@link Gtk.ListBox.set_placeholder}
     * for info.
     * 
     * # Shortcuts and Gestures
     * 
     * The following signals have default keybindings:
     * 
     * - `Gtk.ListBox::move-cursor`
     * - `Gtk.ListBox::select-all`
     * - `Gtk.ListBox::toggle-cursor-row`
     * - `Gtk.ListBox::unselect-all`
     * 
     * # CSS nodes
     * 
     * ```
     * list[.separators][.rich-list][.navigation-sidebar][.boxed-list]
     * ╰── row[.activatable]
     * ```
     * 
     * {@link Gtk.ListBox} uses a single CSS node named list. It may carry the .separators
     * style class, when the {@link Gtk.ListBox.show_separators} property is set.
     * Each {@link Gtk.ListBoxRow} uses a single CSS node named row. The row nodes get the
     * .activatable style class added when appropriate.
     * 
     * It may also carry the .boxed-list style class. In this case, the list will be
     * automatically surrounded by a frame and have separators.
     * 
     * The main list node may also carry style classes to select
     * the style of [list presentation](https://docs.gtk.org/gtk4/section-list-widget.html#list-styles):
     * .rich-list, .navigation-sidebar or .data-table.
     * 
     * # Accessibility
     * 
     * {@link Gtk.ListBox} uses the {@link Gtk.AccessibleRole.LIST} role and {@link Gtk.ListBoxRow} uses
     * the {@link Gtk.AccessibleRole.LIST_ITEM} role.
     * @gir-type Class
     */
